// Auto-generated from legacy HTML by scripts/extract-pages.py
export const title = "Luxriot Evo Integration Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Luxriot Evo Integration Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n<h3>1.1 Prerequisites</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>AIBridge FW version 103808 or later.</li>\n<li>Luxriot Evo S / Global VMS version 1.22 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>1.2 Understanding the Integration Architecture</h3>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 380\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <rect x=\"560\" y=\"30\" width=\"180\" height=\"90\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dbe6fb\" stroke=\"#8ea9df\"/>\n  <text x=\"650\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1b3a7a\" font-weight=\"700\">Luxriot</text>\n  <text x=\"650\" y=\"85\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#1b3a7a\">Client, Mobile App</text>\n  <rect x=\"560\" y=\"160\" width=\"180\" height=\"70\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dbe6fb\" stroke=\"#8ea9df\"/>\n  <text x=\"650\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#1b3a7a\" font-weight=\"700\">Luxriot</text>\n  <line x1=\"650\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"650\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrL)\" marker-start=\"url(#arrL)\"/>\n  <text x=\"660\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#5b6270\">Object Metadata / Event Notification</text>\n  <rect x=\"30\" y=\"150\" width=\"150\" height=\"70\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f6cfcf\" stroke=\"#c98a8a\"/>\n  <text x=\"105\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#5c2626\" font-weight=\"700\">IP Cameras</text>\n  <line x1=\"180\" y1=\"175\" x2=\"555\" y2=\"175\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrL)\"/>\n  <text x=\"360\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <rect x=\"270\" y=\"290\" width=\"180\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#3a3f4a\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n  <text x=\"360\" y=\"325\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\" font-weight=\"700\">AIBridge</text>\n  <line x1=\"105\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"290\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrL)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"450\" y1=\"300\" x2=\"640\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#e07a3f\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrL)\" marker-start=\"url(#arrL)\"/>\n  <text x=\"560\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#e07a3f\">External Service (HTTP API) &#8211; AI Metadata &amp; Event</text>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrL\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f9c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>IP cameras send video streams to both Luxriot VMS and AIBridge</figcaption>\n</div>\n<p>IP cameras send video streams to the Luxriot VMS and to AIBridge.</p>\n<p>AIBridge analyzes the video stream it receives through its AI apps and sends the resulting metadata and events to the Evo VMS.</p>\n<p>AIBridge also responds to search requests made from the Evo VMS.</p>\n\n<h2>2. Configuration</h2>\n<h3>2.1 Configure AIBridge</h3>\n<p>Add an AI app setting. Select the app you want from Explore AI Apps.</p>\n<p>(This guide uses LPR as an example, but you can register an action handler for any of the 50+ apps AIBridge supports.)</p>\n<p>Click the <strong>Add Rule</strong> button.</p>\n<p>Configure the AI app's zone or detail settings.</p>\n<p>Add a Luxriot plugin action setting.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:420px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:90px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Action Setting</span><span class=\"btn small primary\">Add</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Select <strong>Luxriot</strong> from the action type list. (Under VMS: NX Plugin, Luxriot, Milestone, Genetec, Avigilon, exacqVision; under NVR/DVR: Sequrinet, and more.)</p>\n<p>Click the <strong>Add Luxriot Action</strong> button, then click <strong>Edit</strong> next to the server field.</p>\n<p>Enter the Evo VMS info (IP address, web port, username, password). Use the <strong>Login</strong> button to confirm the Evo VMS settings are correct.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:420px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:110px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>IP Address</span><input value=\"192.168.76.62\" disabled>\n    <span>Web Port</span><input value=\"8080\" disabled>\n    <span>User</span><input value=\"admin\" disabled>\n    <span>Password</span><input type=\"password\" value=\"********\" disabled>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"margin-top:10px;display:flex;gap:10px;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <label><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled> Use Recording Server</label>\n    <label><input type=\"checkbox\" checked disabled> Send Metadata</label>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. When Metadata Enable is turned on, AIBridge sends AI-detected object metadata to the Evo VMS. In environments with many detected objects, this can cause performance issues where the AI app is installed.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. If a Luxriot Evo Global user has registered a device using Evo Recording, check <strong>Use Recording Server</strong> and enter the recording server's IP address and web port. This option is not required for Luxriot Evo S.</p>\n\n<h3>2.2 AIBridge Channel Mapping</h3>\n<p>Set the relationship between AIBridge channels and Evo VMS channels. Click the <strong>Mapping</strong> button to open the setup pop-up.</p>\n<p>Enter the recording identifier (UUID) of the channel registered in the Evo VMS into AIBridge.</p>\n<p>The recording identifier (UUID) can be found in the channel's <strong>Details</strong> menu in the Evo Management Console.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>Channel</th><th>Recording Identifier (UUID)</th><th>AIBridge Channel</th><th>Status</th></tr>\n<tr><td>1</td><td>D3A5CBBC-0261-4192-95F4-23B7AEC2428B</td><td>AI Bridge 1</td><td>Connected</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2</td><td>430E946A-BA11-4211-8F51-35F30185B113</td><td>AI Bridge 2</td><td>Connected</td></tr>\n<tr><td>&#8230;</td><td>&#8230;</td><td>&#8230;</td><td>&#8230;</td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p>Enter the recording identifier (UUID) and click <strong>Camera Refresh</strong> to verify it was entered correctly. Once a channel connects successfully, a green <strong>Connected</strong> label is shown.</p>\n\n<h3>2.3 Create the Evo External Service</h3>\n<p>On AIBridge's Evo VMS Setup page, click <strong>Create</strong> to generate the external service.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. Clicking Create resets the channel mapping, so it must be re-mapped afterward. Rule settings and other configuration are not reset.</p>\n<p>Next, create the external service group in the Evo Management Console (<strong>Configuration &gt; External services &gt; New external service group</strong>).</p>\n<p>Enter <strong>AI Bridge</strong> as the name of the new external service group.</p>\n<p>Assign the AIBridge external service to the new external service group.</p>\n<p>Under the channel's <strong>Video analytics</strong> settings, enable the <strong>External metadata</strong> and <strong>External service metadata</strong> checkboxes.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. If you are using an Evo Recording Server, select it under the server settings.</p>\n<p>Under <strong>Configuration &gt; Recording</strong>, enable the <strong>VCA stream</strong> option in the recording profile.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. To use the external service, external use must be enabled in each channel's configuration individually. This setting needs to be configured per channel.</p>\n\n<h3>2.4 Configure the Event Action Message</h3>\n<p>The event action message setting lets you configure the format of the message sent to Luxriot when an event occurs in AI Bridge. For example, adding LPR info or counting data to the message lets you see it in Luxriot.</p>\n<p>When configuring the event action message, you can choose between two content types: Text and Key-Value. Firmware versions before 13907 have no content-type option and always operate in Text mode. Text mode is not recommended for Luxriot compatibility, so this guide describes the Key-Value method. To use Key-Value mode, upgrade the firmware to 13907 or later.</p>\n<p>Select <strong>Key-Value</strong> as the content type, then configure the event action message. Choose the string composition you want, then click <strong>Set Default</strong> to configure the event action message.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:520px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:120px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Content-Type</span><select disabled><option>Key-Value (Recommended)</option></select>\n    <span>String Composition</span><select disabled><option>Basic Info + LPR</option></select>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"section-label\">Event Action Message</div>\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:110px 1fr auto;font-size:12px;\">\n    <span>Event Name</span><input value=\"{{event_name}}\" disabled><span>&#128465;</span>\n    <span>LP Number</span><input value=\"{{object_list}}{{object.lp_text}}\" disabled><span>&#128465;</span>\n    <span>LP Note</span><input value=\"{{object_list}}{{object.lp_note}}\" disabled><span>&#128465;</span>\n    <span>LP Group Name</span><input value=\"{{object_list}}{{object.lp_groups}}\" disabled><span>&#128465;</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. Keys and their values are shown in the Live view as in the example below. If a value is empty, its key is not shown either.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. Cortrol has a known multi-language issue, so some characters may render incorrectly.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. The keys you enter appear as search result columns in Luxriot.</p>\n<p>Click <strong>Confirm</strong> to save the Evo action setting.</p>\n<p>If a device is registered under the External Service tab in the Evo Management Console in the format <strong>AIBridge-MacAddress</strong>, the setup is correct.</p>\n\n<h3>2.5 Create Evo Events and Rules</h3>\n<p>You need to configure the events, actions, and rules that will deliver alerts.</p>\n<p>To add a new event, click the <strong>New Event</strong> button.</p>\n<p>Set the event type to <strong>External Event &#8211; External Service</strong>.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:460px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:110px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Event type</span><input value=\"External service\" disabled>\n    <span>Title</span><input value=\"test 1 External service\" disabled>\n    <span>Source</span><input value=\"test 1\" disabled>\n    <span>Service group</span><input value=\"AI Bridge\" disabled>\n    <span>Target event</span><select disabled><option>Event</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. The Target Event section lists the events currently used on AI Bridge. If you want to receive alerts for every event, select <strong>Event</strong>.</p>\n<p>Combine the event type you created with an action to build a rule, using the <strong>Open configurator</strong> button under Events Actions &gt; Rules.</p>\n\n<h2>3. Demo</h2>\n<h3>3.1 Live</h3>\n<p>Set up the Evo Client to display metadata and alarms to confirm the integration with AIBridge is working correctly.</p>\n<p>Clicking the bell-shaped icon at the bottom of the video lets you check the real-time Event Log on the live screen.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. In the event action message, the key you entered is shown together with its value. If a value is empty, the corresponding key is not shown either.</p>\n\n<h3>3.2 Search</h3>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. In the event action message, the key you entered becomes a column, and its corresponding value is shown in that column.</p>\n<p>You can use the Keyword field to search for LPR values or attributes.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. Searches match on partial license plate numbers, not just full matches, and are not case-sensitive.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. Keyword searches match against Values, not Keys.</p>\n\n<h2>4. FAQ</h2>\n<h3>4.1 Object Metadata Transmission Option</h3>\n<p>If this feature is turned off, ONVIF metadata and metadata configured in the plugin are not transmitted. This applies to metadata transmission as a whole.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:460px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:60px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Ch 1</span><select disabled><option>Event Objects Only</option></select>\n    <span>Ch 2</span><select disabled><option>Event Objects Only</option></select>\n  </div>\n  <label style=\"display:block;margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;\"><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled> Ignore static objects &#8212; static objects are not sent when transmitting metadata.</label>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>(Home &gt; Output &gt; Object Meta Info; mode options per channel: All Objects / Event Objects Only / Do Not Send.)</p>\n\n<h3>4.2 Video Analytics Overlay Setting on the Evo Client Side</h3>\n<p>If Video Analytics is not enabled in the Edit settings of the Evo Client Application, metadata may not work correctly. This is set to ON by default, so do not turn this feature off.</p>\n\n<h3>4.3 Verifying the Connection Between AIBridge and Luxriot Evo</h3>\n<p>Click <strong>Event Rule Map</strong> under Video in the left menu of the AI Bridge webpage.</p>\n<p>Select the <strong>Action Presets</strong> tab, then click the edit button on the Luxriot setting you configured earlier.</p>\n<p>Once you confirm the connection to the Luxriot server is shown, click the <strong>Test</strong> button.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. Before clicking Test, confirm the Evo server shows a green Connected label. If it shows gray Disconnected, check the server settings.</p>\n<p>After clicking Test, a success pop-up appears once the message is sent successfully: <em>\"A test event has been sent. Please check the event.\"</em></p>\n<p>Now go to Luxriot Evo and check the alarm message.</p>\n\n<h3>4.4 How to Display Object IDs in Luxriot Evo</h3>\n<p>To check the ID of each channel or object in Luxriot Evo, you need to enable an option in Luxriot Evo. Follow the steps below.</p>\n<p>Open the Luxriot Evo Console app, click the button in the top right corner, then click <strong>Settings</strong>.</p>\n<p>Click <strong>Show object IDs</strong>, then click the <strong>OK</strong> button.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <label style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:12.5px;\"><input type=\"checkbox\" checked disabled> Show object IDs &nbsp; <span style=\"color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;\">This setting controls visibility of object IDs</span></label>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Once applied correctly, you can see IDs on every object under Devices, Servers, Channels, and more.</p>\n\n<h2>5. Revision History</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>Version</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.00</td><td>Initial document.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.10</td><td>Added images and supplemental content to Section 2, Configuration.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.20</td><td>Updated content related to compatible versions.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.30</td><td>Added content and updated images in Section 2.1, Configure AIBridge.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.40</td><td>Updated the Event Action Message feature.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.50</td><td>Added FAQ 4.4.</td></tr>\n</table>";
